  "notes": {
    "carplayNote": {
      "color": "orange",
      "text": "Status tab: CPInformationTemplate — title, text/detail rows and buttons. Colors, fonts and layout belong to the system. The colored dot stands in for the status marker the app puts in the title today. Tabs: CPTabBarTemplate with Status, Map, Details.",
      "w": 320,
      "x": 3520,
      "y": 1224
    },
    "detailsNote": {
      "color": "orange",
      "text": "Variant A: CPPointOfInterestTemplate — a real MapKit map, up to 12 pins (regions under alert) and a list panel; selecting a pin shows a card with up to 2 buttons. Pro: native, pan/zoom, allowed for driving task apps. Con: pins instead of colored oblasts; Apple says driving task apps must not be location finders — review risk. Gray silhouette = stand-in for MapKit.",
      "w": 340,
      "x": 1760,
      "y": 2084
    },
    "launchNote": {
      "color": "blue",
      "text": "One shape, three places: icon (Mark), launch screen and the Status hero share the tick ring and disc, so launch → status is a single continuous motion.\n\nRules: the launch dot is neutral (status unknown). Sweep = Checking while the first fetch runs; with fresh cached status (refresh-policy) skip the sweep and go straight to the disc. Never wait for the animation to show data: total added time ≤ 400 ms after status is known. Reduce Motion: cross-fade launch → Status.\n\nBuild: UILaunchScreen can only center an image, so either use a LaunchScreen storyboard with the mark pinned to the hero position (ring top 116 pt from the screen top on a 390×844 phone), or center the mark and move it up as part of the animation.",
      "w": 520,
      "x": 940,
      "y": 6204
    },
    "mapBNote": {
      "color": "orange",
      "text": "Variant B: CPListTemplate with the Ubilling ?map= raster as a list image (same picture as the phone map card). Pro: colored oblasts, same free signal as the phone, no new data. Con: image size is capped by the car (maximumImageSize), not pannable; landscape list images are new in iOS 27 and must be checked for driving task apps. Gray silhouette = stand-in for the raster.",
      "w": 340,
      "x": 1760,
      "y": 2944
    },
    "missingScreensNote": {
      "color": "blue",
      "text": "DS-3 mockups. Binding numbers, states and copy live in the repo (spec by drivecheck-product); this row mirrors them.\n\nPlaceholders in [brackets] come from StoreKit at runtime (plan names, prices, renewal date).\n\nCopy marked as proposals in the DS-3 report is not in the String Catalog yet.",
      "w": 420,
      "x": 4230,
      "y": 7280
    },
